Non-negotiables for every task. Details and examples: playwright-conventions.mdc (tests) and qa-orchestrator.mdc (ticket/CI workflow) — both added later.

## MUST

| Rule | Notes |
|------|-------|
| Role-based locators | getByRole → getByLabel → getByText; getByTestId only when nothing user-facing fits |
| Web-first assertions | expect(locator)…; never snapshot booleans (isVisible(), textContent()) |
| storageState auth | Log in once per family in the setup project; credentials from process.env |
| Unique, self-cleaning data | Date.now() or a factory per test; API teardown |
| One tag per test | Exactly one of @smoke @sanity @regression @api @e2e @destructive on each test(); never on describe() |

## SHOULD

| Practice | Notes |
|----------|-------|
| Faker factories | Shared builders for names, emails, payloads, not inline magic strings |
| Enums for repeated strings | Roles, routes, labels used in 2+ places |
| JSDoc on POM action methods | Brief @param / return on user-facing flows in pages/ |
| Composition over BasePage | A HeaderComponent class that each page holds rather than inherits. LoginPage has a header property that is a HeaderComponent. Do it instead of the classic BasePage |

## WON'T

| Forbidden | Why |
|-----------|-----|
| XPath | Brittle, not user-facing |
| waitForTimeout | Guesses a duration; use web-first expect |
| Hardcoded secrets | Use process.env; the auth files are git-ignored |
| The any type | Defeats TypeScript safety in fixtures and POMs |
| Weakened assertions | No deleting, softening, or commenting out expect() to go green |
| Healing a real bug | Triage first; drift → self-heal; product defect → bug-reporter |
| Tags on describe | Tags belong on individual test() blocks only |
| Inheritance (the classic BasePage) | LoginPage extends BasePage. Subclasses inherit the header element and its methods. |

